Pawlak was selected as the party's candidate. He was challenged most prominently by [[Józef Zych]] at the party's convention, however, Zych resigned from seeking the candidacy.<ref>{{cite news |title=PSL zwleka ze zgłoszeniem kandydata |url=https://archiwum.rp.pl/artykul/55596-PSL-zwleka-ze-zgloszeniem-kandydata.html |access-date=2025-03-24}}</ref><ref>{{cite news |title=Waldemar Pawlak kandydatem PSL na prezydenta  |url=https://www.newsweek.pl/polska/waldemar-pawlak-kandydatem-psl-na-prezydenta-w-wyborach-2010/gm4hktp |access-date=2025-03-24}}</ref><ref name=Dudek/> A poll conducted in December 1994 suggested 68% of potential PSL voters supported Pawlak as the party's candidate, 1% supported [[Janusz Piechociński]] and 9% supported Zych.<ref name=CBOS1/>

